rase introduces a set T and states that g is continuous on T, while the informal problem specifies continuity for x > e^e.\"], \"paraphrase\": \"For all real numbers x greater than exp(exp(1)), the sequence S(x, n) defined by S(x, 0) = exp(1) and S(x, n+1) = log_{S(x, n)}(x) converges to a limit L as n approaches infinity. Additionally, if this sequence also converges to g(x) for all x in T, then the function g is continuous on T.\", \"comparison_status\": \"completed\"}}"
